## Package writer, files and notices

The implementation to inspect is `tools/handover/package.mjs`. There is no
separate export-source or ruby-map tool at this pin: the writer generates
`RUBY-MAP.md` itself. Its held invocation is:

```text
node tools/handover/package.mjs tmp/<new-package-directory> --engine-commit <accepted-full-engine-commit>
```

Do not run it during this documentation task. Later execution requires the
actual clean packaging checkout and a new destination below its `tmp/`.
Do not use `--allow-dirty` for an accepted package. The writer reads tracked
working files/index modes, not merely the commit named in a report.

- [ ] Inspect the exact selected surface: `src/`, vendored libraries/notices,
      migration/schema/seed files, distribution and migration tools, reference
      runner/TS adapter, synthetic-v1 and write-battery-v1, schema declarations,
      the selected host/config/compiler helpers, and TinyMCE corresponding source.
- [ ] Inspect generated root documents: README, PORT-SCOPE, DIFFERENCES, NOTICE,
      KNOWN-COMPARISON-FAILURE, RUBY-MAP and HANDOVER-MANIFEST. Package scripts are
      rewritten: `npm test` becomes the package smoke check, not correctness.
- [ ] Verify every manifest path, Git mode, byte length and SHA256 against the
      actual output; distinguish `sourceCommit` from `engineCommit`. Check the
      generated Ruby map includes uncited modules and difference annotations.
- [ ] Retain LICENSE and component grants/provenance, including HTML extraction
      dependencies, Uglifier inputs, LibSass source/WASM, CodeRay, kramdown,
      ActiveSupport/Haml, fonts and bundled assets. Check TinyMCE 5.10.7 source,
      manifests, upstream license/build inputs and bundled-byte binding using
      `tools/handover/tinymce-export-custody.mjs`; source presence is not a
      completed redistribution review.
- [ ] Complete independent content/source-supply review. Exclude credentials,
      real decks/uploads, withheld fixtures, development Git history and private
      deployment material. The writer's pattern scan is insufficient by itself;
      a blocked scan can still leave output bytes, which must not be shared.
- [ ] Verify native POSIX permissions where claimed. Windows records Git modes
      without proving executable bits on a POSIX filesystem.

