## Supported intent and open gates

The proposed local recipe is Node plus SQLite with synthetic fixtures. Driver
source for other databases is not verified deployment support. Arbitrary Ruby
gems, native extensions, Rails/HAML views, all mods, private migration inputs,
original-password access, hosted providers, mail/jobs and production cutover
need their own evidence. The shared contract requires first-class Ruby and
TypeScript implementations; this package does not establish that acceptance
or retire Ruby.

Package construction/readback, no-Git build, install/native-module checks,
local host lifecycle, migration/recovery, the package's own category
comparison, source-supply/privacy/permissions review and exact publication
approval remain open for this draft. The development-tree category comparison
has passed (2026-11-02, candidate b75d7bbb: rendering 1754/1754, semantics
2389/2389, persistence 16/16, side effects 19/19). No performance, cost, energy or overall compatibility
claim is made. See the companion Ruby mapping and `docs/core/governance.md`.
